  "source_commit": "7cbf7a0c32fca1badf05931879a37c3f8a2b03b4",
  "scope": "Focused complete mathematical/source-contract review of LGS9-LGS11; LGS1-LGS8 and the cited immutable EL/JR/LW/LC/SR statements are inherited inputs, not re-proved in this review. No construction of the common compatibility record or selected tops is inferred.",
  "findings": [
    "LGS9: actual vOf injection identifies distinct commuting coordinates; LPprime depth ceil(tv), Dp, kappa and cstar=8(Dp+1) match the original source. The actual polar/predual slot is used, so the normalized p^A edge pairing has the correct w^2=p cancellation. JR4-JR7 hypotheses are discharged by LGS8 and EL5-EL10; exceptional tensor directions multiply and errors lie at the stated depth.",
    "LGS10: served nonempty implies exactly goodReps at a candidate with Sig<=x^-epsilon. The source Sv is already an integer ceiling of a nonnegative sum; tauP is precisely ep plus the integer walk depth. The Mna-to-M shift preserves counts, Smith tails give e_O*d*(tau+S*(prod(1+m*kappa)-1)), and exp(Sigma)-1<=2Sigma yields exact ioP. Empty served set and S=0 are checked separately. Saturation follows from Vram being the coefficient-field span, so intersection with p^tau M is p^tau Mram.",
    "LGS11: Chain has only linear Kz fields; m>=2 ensures the zero composite. Every vGeLat condition holds with any DVR uniformizer. Direct source comparison confirms LatTied, yProd, NP, LatticeLengthsAtPlace and all five LinkG fields do not depend on Ch. Original Extra.ker is explicitly not transported; this matches AdmissibleFamilyNoKernel and preserves the geometric chain."
  ],
